  "从测量可信度到过程与寿命判断": "From Measurement Confidence to Capability & Life",
  "报告把测量系统、尺寸能力、过程风险和弯折寿命分开分析，再讨论它们如何共同影响零件质量。": "The report analyses measurement systems, dimensional capability, process risk and bending life separately, then considers how they jointly affect part quality.",
  "01 先检查数据能否支持判断": "01 Check whether the data support the assessment",
  "每个尺寸采用 10 个零件、3 名操作者、每人重复测量 3 次的交叉设计。Gage R&R 用于区分重复性、再现性与零件间变异，ndc 用于辅助判断区分零件的能力。厚度结果可以支持后续讨论；宽度和长度应优先改善定位、接触方式与重复测量的一致性。": "Each dimension used a crossed design with 10 parts, 3 operators and 3 repeated measurements per operator. Gage R&R separates repeatability, reproducibility and part-to-part variation; ndc helps assess the ability to distinguish between parts. The thickness results support further discussion. Width and length first require improvements to locating, contact method and consistency of repeated measurements.",
  "02 将能力指标接回制造过程": "02 Link capability metrics to the manufacturing process",
  "厚度 Ppk 约 0.35、Cpk 约 0.27，提示该样本过程能力不足。报告进一步用过程图、FMEA 和鱼骨图整理切片、材料干燥、温控及测量等因素，把失效模式、潜在原因和预防检查措施对应起来。能力数值用于定位问题，不能单独证明是哪一个打印参数造成偏差。": "Thickness Ppk of approximately 0.35 and Cpk of approximately 0.27 indicated insufficient process capability in this sample. The report then used a process map, FMEA and fishbone diagram to organise factors including slicing, material drying, temperature control and measurement, linking failure modes to potential causes and preventive checks. Capability metrics help identify problems but cannot, on their own, establish which printing parameter caused the deviation.",
  "03 分别验证尺寸质量与耐久性": "03 Validate dimensional quality and durability separately",
  "新旧铰链各 10 件的弯折数据采用 Weibull 模型比较。新组 B10 较高，平均寿命估计却较低，说明早期失效和寿命长尾会给出不同结论。评价新方案时，需要同时看尺寸居中、波动、失效分布与样本量，不能把某个指标改善直接等同于整体可靠性提升。": "Bending data from the original and new hinge groups, with 10 parts each, were compared using Weibull models. The new group had a higher B10 but a lower estimated mean life, showing that early failures and the long-life tail can lead to different conclusions. Evaluating a new design requires consideration of dimensional centring, variation, failure distributions and sample size. Improvement in one metric does not establish better overall reliability.",
