  "团队识别的主要约束": "Main constraint identified by the team",
  "团队如何做决策": "How the Team Made Decisions",
  "以需求预测作为输入，模拟混合、灌装与包装过程，再结合各规格库存、收入和持有成本比较配置。模型以每个 agent 对应 10 L 饮料进行转换，需要持续核对瓶数、升数和产出单位。": "The team used demand forecasts as inputs to simulate mixing, filling and packaging, then compared configurations using inventory by package size, revenue and holding costs. Each model agent represented 10 L of beverage, requiring consistent checks of conversions between bottle counts, litres and output units.",
  "团队判断灌装限制整体产出，因此优先比较灌装资源、产品规格和换型策略，而不是让各道工序平均增加投入。": "The team identified filling as the constraint on total output, so it prioritised comparisons of filling resources, product sizes and changeover strategies rather than increasing resources equally across all processes.",
  "我的分析重点": "My Analysis Focus",
  "短预测窗口响应快，但可能带来频繁换型；长窗口较稳定，却容易跟不上需求变化。我将预测方法局限、生产响应延迟、库存反馈滞后与外部扰动拆开分析，提出改善模型响应与数据衔接的方向。": "Short forecast windows respond quickly but can trigger frequent changeovers. Longer windows are more stable but may lag behind demand changes. I analysed forecasting limitations, production response delays, delayed inventory feedback and external disturbances separately, then proposed ways to improve model responsiveness and data integration.",
  "放大：团队 AnyLogic 生产流程模型，原报告 PDF 第 7 页。": "Enlarge: the team’s AnyLogic production process model, original report, PDF p. 7.",
  "团队 AnyLogic 生产流程模型，原报告 PDF 第 7 页。": "The team’s AnyLogic production process model, original report, PDF p. 7.",
  "放大：Excel 周度产品配置与利润分析表，原报告 PDF 第 10 页。": "Enlarge: Excel weekly product configuration and profit analysis table, original report, PDF p. 10.",
  "Excel 周度产品配置与利润分析表，原报告 PDF 第 10 页。": "Excel weekly product configuration and profit analysis table, original report, PDF p. 10.",
  "预测、产能与库存如何形成周度计划": "Turning Forecasts, Capacity & Inventory into Weekly Plans",
  "团队围绕 9 种产品与包装组合建立 30 周生产决策框架。我主要展开预测不确定性、响应滞后与模型改进分析。": "The team used 9 product–package combinations to develop a 30-week production decision framework. My main analysis covered forecast uncertainty, response delays and model improvements.",
  "01 比较预测方法及其适用条件": "01 Compare forecasting methods and their suitability",
  "报告比较移动平均、加权移动平均和指数平滑，并采用加权移动平均支持需求估计。我的分析关注预测窗口和固定参数的局限：短窗口更快响应近期变化，也容易引起计划调整；长窗口较平稳，却可能滞后于需求。预测误差需要通过库存、缺货与换型后果来理解。": "The report compared moving averages, weighted moving averages and exponential smoothing, and used weighted moving averages to estimate demand. My analysis focused on the limitations of forecast windows and fixed parameters: short windows respond faster to recent changes but can prompt plan revisions; longer windows are steadier but may lag behind demand. Forecast errors need to be understood through their implications for inventory, shortages and changeovers.",
  "02 将不同工序换算到同一产出单位": "02 Compare processes using consistent output units",
  "混合、灌装和包装的资源与处理方式不同。团队将各阶段产能统一比较，并识别灌装为主要约束。模型中的 agent 对应 10 L 饮料，因此瓶数、体积、时间和周度产出之间的转换尤其关键。增加上游产出不一定增加最终交付，还可能造成等待或库存积压。": "Mixing, filling and packaging use different resources and processing methods. The team compared capacity across stages on a common basis and identified filling as the main constraint. Each model agent represented 10 L of beverage, making conversions between bottle counts, volume, time and weekly output particularly important. Increasing upstream output does not necessarily increase final deliveries and may instead create waiting or inventory buildup.",
  "03 连接生产配置与库存反馈": "03 Connect production configuration with inventory feedback",
  "团队通过 AnyLogic 模型和 Excel 配置表比较周度生产、库存和利润。我关注需求预测、生产响应与库存反馈之间的滞后，并提出动态调整参数、考虑换型影响和减少手工传递等方向。现场未按时完成全部 30 周，报告有后续补算，因此保留框架和复盘，不使用未经统一核验的总利润提升。": "The team used the AnyLogic model and Excel configuration tables to compare weekly production, inventory and profit. I focused on delays between demand forecasts, production responses and inventory feedback, proposing dynamic parameter adjustments, consideration of changeover effects and less manual data transfer. Not all 30 weeks were completed within the workshop time; the report includes later calculations. I therefore present the framework and review findings without claiming an overall profit improvement that has not been consistently verified.",
