  "供应链": "Supply chain",
  "← 测量系统与质量可靠性": "← Measurement Systems, Quality & Reliability",
  "五类工艺与尺寸偏差 →": "Five Processes & Dimensional Deviation →",
  "Prusa 零件的五类制造工艺与尺寸偏差分析": "Five Manufacturing Processes and Dimensional Variation in Prusa Parts",
  "个人课程报告": "Individual course report",
  "KIC 关键检验尺寸 · 公差对照 · 工艺比较 · SolidWorks": "Key Inspection Characteristics (KIC) · Tolerance checks · Process comparison · SolidWorks",
  "围绕 Prusa MK3.1 结构件，比较 CNC、金属铸造、PU 浇注、注塑和钣金工艺，讨论原型零件转向批量制造时的尺寸与装配问题。": "Compared CNC machining, metal casting, PU casting, injection moulding and sheet metal fabrication for Prusa MK3.1 structural parts, examining dimensional and assembly issues when moving from prototypes to volume production.",
  "个人报告整理五类零件的关键尺寸检查、名义值与实测值对照，结合实物与工程图比较工艺表现并提出改进建议。": "Prepared an individual report covering key dimension checks and nominal-to-measured comparisons for five types of parts, using physical samples and engineering drawings to compare process performance and propose improvements.",
  "五类工艺的 KIC 尺寸对照、制造性能比较和样件问题分析。": "KIC dimension comparisons across five processes, manufacturing performance comparisons and sample defect analysis.",
  "制造工艺": "Manufacturing processes",
  "关键检验尺寸对照": "Key inspection dimension comparisons",
  "注塑导杆孔相对名义值的偏差": "Injection-moulded guide-rod bore deviation from nominal",
  "从尺寸偏差看装配风险": "Linking dimensional variation to assembly risk",
  "例如注塑 Y 轴导杆夹块的导杆孔：名义值为 8.00 mm，报告实测为 7.71 mm，相差 −0.29 mm。比起仅判断“合格或不合格”，更需要看这个偏差会怎样影响导杆插入、定位与后续装配。": "For example, the guide-rod bore in the injection-moulded Y-axis rod holder had a nominal diameter of 8.00 mm and a reported measurement of 7.71 mm: a deviation of −0.29 mm. Beyond a simple pass/fail judgement, the question is how this difference affects rod insertion, location and subsequent assembly.",
  "比较工艺的取舍": "Comparing process trade-offs",
  "CNC 关注装夹、刀具可达性与加工精度；铸造和注塑关注收缩、模具结构与冷却；钣金关注折弯、孔位与装配关系。报告同时比较加工速度、成本、质量、灵活性与可持续性。": "CNC machining calls for attention to workholding, tool access and machining accuracy; casting and injection moulding to shrinkage, mould design and cooling; and sheet metal fabrication to bends, hole positions and assembly interfaces. The report also compares speed, cost, quality, flexibility and sustainability.",
  "放大：铸造件实物，PDF 第 11 页。": "Enlarge: Metal casting sample, PDF p. 11.",
  "铸造件实物，PDF 第 11 页。": "Metal casting sample, PDF p. 11.",
  "放大：钣金件实物，PDF 第 21 页。": "Enlarge: Sheet metal sample, PDF p. 21.",
  "钣金件实物，PDF 第 21 页。": "Sheet metal sample, PDF p. 21.",
  "放大：PU 浇注零件实物，PDF 第 14 页。": "Enlarge: PU casting sample, PDF p. 14.",
  "PU 浇注零件实物，PDF 第 14 页。": "PU casting sample, PDF p. 14.",
  "从关键尺寸到制造工艺取舍": "From critical dimensions to process trade-offs",
  "通过五类制造工艺的实物与工程图对照，理解尺寸偏差如何传递到装配、功能和工艺选择。": "Compared physical samples with engineering drawings across five manufacturing processes to understand how dimensional variation affects assembly, function and process selection.",
  "01 先确定关键尺寸对应什么功能": "01 Link critical dimensions to function",
  "KIC 检查围绕孔径、孔距、间隙、位置和垂直度等展开。名义尺寸与实测值的差异需要与导杆插入、轴承定位、皮带运行或电机安装等具体功能相联系。例如注塑导杆孔由名义 8.00 mm 测得 7.71 mm，首先要讨论它是否影响导杆插入与定位。": "KIC checks covered bore diameter, hole spacing, clearance, position and perpendicularity. Differences between nominal and measured dimensions must be linked to specific functions, such as guide-rod insertion, bearing location, belt travel or motor mounting. For example, a nominal 8.00 mm injection-moulded guide-rod bore measured 7.71 mm; the first question is whether this affects rod insertion and location.",
  "02 比较五类工艺各自的限制": "02 Compare the constraints of five processes",
  "CNC 零件重点看基准、装夹和刀具可达性；铸造与注塑重点看收缩、模具及冷却；PU 浇注还需要注意模具定位与变形；钣金则要把展开、折弯、回弹和安装孔关系放在一起考虑。报告同时比较速度、成本、质量、灵活性和可持续性，避免只凭单个尺寸选择工艺。": "For CNC parts, the focus was on datums, workholding and tool access; for casting and injection moulding, on shrinkage, mould design and cooling. PU casting also required attention to mould alignment and deformation. Sheet metal fabrication required consideration of flat patterns, bending, springback and mounting-hole relationships together. The report compares speed, cost, quality, flexibility and sustainability to avoid selecting a process based on a single dimension.",
  "03 区分异常读数与已确认根因": "03 Separate unusual readings from confirmed causes",
  "报告中的尺寸对照可以支持问题定位，但单次测量不能独立证明原因。对显著偏差，应先检查测量基准、接触位置和记录，再安排重复测量。只有排除测量影响后，才进一步验证收缩补偿、装夹重复性、冷却或回弹等工艺假设。": "The dimensional comparisons help locate problems, but a single measurement cannot establish a cause. Large deviations first require checks of the measurement datum, contact position and recording, followed by repeat measurements. Only after measurement effects are ruled out should process hypotheses, such as shrinkage compensation, workholding repeatability, cooling or springback, be investigated.",
  "检查链条": "Inspection sequence",
  "要回答的问题": "Questions to answer",
  "名义尺寸与实测值": "Nominal and measured dimensions",
  "偏差方向和大小是什么？测量口径是否一致？": "What are the direction and magnitude of the deviation? Were measurements taken on a consistent basis?",
