  "KFC Carlton 排队与服务资源仿真": "KFC Carlton Queueing and Service Resource Simulation",
  "课程仿真报告": "Coursework simulation report",
  "AnyLogic · 顾客行为 · 队列 · 情景比较": "AnyLogic · Customer behaviour · Queues · Scenario comparison",
  "将顾客到达、点餐、等待、取餐和离开拆成流程，观察前台、自助点餐与后厨资源如何共同影响等待。": "The model separates customer arrivals, ordering, waiting, collection and departure into process steps to examine how counter service, self-service ordering and kitchen resources jointly affect waiting times.",
  "报告展示 AnyLogic 模型构建、顾客状态逻辑、队列可视化和改善情景分析，重点是用流程与资源配置解释服务拥堵。": "The report presents an AnyLogic model, customer state logic, queue visualisations and improvement scenarios, focusing on how processes and resource allocation explain service congestion.",
  "点餐和取餐流程模型、队列曲线，以及窗口与分流情景比较。": "Models of ordering and collection, queue plots, and comparisons of service-counter and customer-routing scenarios.",
  "点餐路径": "Ordering routes",
  "前台窗口的情景设置": "Service counters in the scenarios",
  "多队列": "Multiple queues",
  "点餐、取餐与就餐状态": "Ordering, collection and dining states",
  "从流程识别约束": "Identify constraints through the process",
  "模型区分前台和电子点餐路径，并考虑顾客到达率、服务时间、座位、前台窗口与后厨工位。观察不同状态下的队列长度，而不是只用餐厅总人数判断拥堵。": "The model distinguishes counter ordering from electronic ordering and accounts for customer arrival rates, service times, seats, service counters and kitchen stations. It examines queue lengths in different states rather than using total restaurant occupancy alone to assess congestion.",
  "比较改善情景": "Compare improvement scenarios",
  "报告讨论增加窗口、自助点餐分流和取餐路径优化。相应记录包含高峰等待时间由 12 分钟到 8 分钟的模拟对比，用于说明方案比较思路。": "The report discusses additional counters, routing customers to self-service ordering and improving collection routes. The recorded scenarios include a simulated comparison of peak waiting time from 12 minutes to 8 minutes, illustrating the approach to comparing options.",
  "放大：点餐、取餐队列与就餐人数的模拟曲线，来自原 Word 报告。": "Enlarge: Simulated ordering and collection queues and dining occupancy, from the original Word report.",
  "点餐、取餐队列与就餐人数的模拟曲线，来自原 Word 报告。": "Simulated ordering and collection queues and dining occupancy, from the original Word report.",
  "顾客状态、资源约束与改善情景": "Customer states, resource constraints and improvement scenarios",
  "将服务系统拆成顾客状态与资源占用，观察点餐、取餐和就餐环节如何共同形成等待。": "The service system is broken down into customer states and resource use to examine how ordering, collection and dining jointly create waiting.",
  "01 将顾客路径转成模型逻辑": "01 Translate customer journeys into model logic",
  "报告区分前台点餐和电子点餐两条路径，并使用顾客代理表达进入、排队、点餐、等待、取餐和离开等状态。前台窗口、后厨工位和座位会分别约束状态转换。这样可以分开观察点餐队列与取餐等待，避免只看餐厅内人数就判断系统拥堵。": "The report distinguishes counter ordering from electronic ordering and uses customer agents to represent entry, queueing, ordering, waiting, collection and departure. Service counters, kitchen stations and seats constrain the transitions between these states. This allows ordering queues and collection waits to be examined separately, avoiding an assessment of congestion based solely on the number of people inside the restaurant.",
  "02 比较资源配置，而不只增加人数": "02 Compare resource allocation beyond adding staff",
  "报告讨论前台窗口由 3 个增至 5 个、自助点餐分流和取餐路径优化。评价这些情景时，需要同时观察前台和后厨：前台排队缩短后，瓶颈可能转移到备餐或取餐环节。12 到 8 分钟是报告中的情景对比，用于展示比较方法，不作为真实门店已实现的改善。": "The report discusses increasing service counters from 3 to 5, routing customers to self-service ordering and improving collection routes. These scenarios require joint assessment of the counter and kitchen: a shorter ordering queue may shift the bottleneck to food preparation or collection. The 12-to-8-minute result is a scenario comparison from the report that illustrates the method; it is not an improvement demonstrated in an operating store.",
  "03 明确下一步怎样核验模型": "03 Define the next model-validation steps",
  "继续验证时，应统一高峰和非高峰客流、服务时间和资源数量，核对顾客是否会重复排队或提前离开。随后在相同输入条件下比较方案，并进行重复运行，记录等待时间、队列长度和资源利用情况。原始输入记录与重复试验不足时，结论应保留在课程模型范围内。": "Further validation should establish consistent peak and off-peak arrival inputs, service times and resource counts, and check whether customers can rejoin queues or leave early. Options should then be compared under identical input conditions, with repeated runs recording waiting times, queue lengths and resource utilisation. Where original input records and replicated experiments are insufficient, conclusions should remain within the scope of the coursework model.",
