  "结果如何使用": "How to use the results",
  "原文包含高峰 120 人/小时与模型 200 人/小时两种客流描述，并缺少可复跑模型及完整随机重复记录。因此 12→8 分钟仅作为报告中的情景结果，不视作已经验证的门店改善。": "The original report describes both peak arrivals of 120 customers/hour and model arrivals of 200 customers/hour, and lacks a rerunnable model and complete records of stochastic replications. The 12→8-minute comparison is therefore presented only as a reported scenario result, not a validated store improvement.",
  "进一步验证应统一客流和服务时间假设，明确等待时间的统计区间，进行重复试验，再比较窗口、人力、后厨和空间约束的整体影响。": "Further validation should reconcile arrival and service-time assumptions, define the interval over which waiting time is measured and run repeated experiments before comparing the combined effects of counters, staffing, kitchen resources and space constraints.",
  "课程服务系统研究，展示模型逻辑与资源配置情景。模拟结果需要统一输入并进行重复试验后，才能用于现场决策。": "A coursework study of a service system, demonstrating model logic and resource-allocation scenarios. Simulation results require consistent inputs and repeated experiments before they can support operational decisions on site.",
  "下载 Word 原报告 ": "Download original Word report ",
  "← 鼠标生命周期与成本": "← Mouse Life Cycle and Cost",
  "Toyota 供应链研究 →": "Toyota Supply Chain Study →",
  "Toyota 供应链战略、数字化与韧性研究": "Toyota Supply Chain Strategy, Digitalisation and Resilience",
  "课程小组案例研究": "Group coursework case study",
  "JIT / Kanban · MTS / MTO · EDI · 风险与可持续性": "JIT / Kanban · MTS / MTO · EDI · Risk and sustainability",
  "通过案例与文献梳理生产策略、供应商协作、数字技术和风险响应，分析信息如何支持物料流与生产决策。": "The study draws on cases and literature to examine production strategy, supplier collaboration, digital technology and risk response, analysing how information supports material flows and production decisions.",
  "按小组会议记录，我负责引言、Toyota 供应链数字化分析、总结，以及全文结构和内容核对。": "As recorded in the team meeting notes, I was responsible for the introduction, analysis of Toyota's supply chain digitalisation, conclusion, and checks of the full report's structure and content.",
  "数字技术分析、供应链研究整合及全文结构与内容核对。": "Digital technology analysis, integration of the supply chain research, and checks of the full report's structure and content.",
  "研究维度": "Research dimensions",
  "数字化": "Digitalisation",
  "个人主要分析内容": "My main area of analysis",
  "案例研究": "Case study",
  "文献与公开材料基础": "Based on literature and public sources",
  "研究结构": "Research structure",
  "团队从生产策略、战略合作、数字化、全球供应链风险和可持续性五个方面展开。讨论拉动与看板、MTS/MTO 的组合以及供应商协同，把库存、交期、响应与风险放到同一框架中。": "The team examined five areas: production strategy, strategic partnerships, digitalisation, global supply chain risks and sustainability. The discussion covers pull systems and Kanban, combinations of MTS/MTO and supplier coordination, bringing inventory, lead times, responsiveness and risk into a shared framework.",
  "我的研究输出": "My research contribution",
  "围绕数字技术如何服务信息同步、可视化、预测和异常响应展开分析，并把这些内容与报告其他部分衔接；同时核对结构、引言与总结的一致性。": "I analysed how digital technologies support information synchronisation, visibility, forecasting and exception response, and linked this analysis to the report's other sections. I also checked consistency across the structure, introduction and conclusion.",
  "个人负责的研究重点": "My research focus",
  "技术如何支持": "How technology supports",
  "供应链决策": "supply chain decisions",
  "技术方向": "Technology area",
  "分析中的用途": "Application in the analysis",
  "EDI 与信息共享": "EDI and information sharing",
  "订单、补货与交期协同": "Coordination of orders, replenishment and delivery timing",
  "物料状态与追溯": "Material status and traceability",
  "数字孪生": "Digital twins",
  "情景评估与风险响应": "Scenario assessment and risk response",
  "AI 与分析工具": "AI and analytics tools",
  "需求预测与异常识别": "Demand forecasting and anomaly detection",
  "按报告研究框架整理，表示分析用途。": "Organised using the report's research framework to show the applications discussed.",
  "从供应链问题选择数字化与协同方法": "Choose digital and collaborative methods around supply chain problems",
  "这是基于公开资料的课程研究。我负责引言、数字化分析、总结，以及全文结构和内容的衔接核对。": "This coursework study is based on public sources. I was responsible for the introduction, digitalisation analysis, conclusion, and checks of the full report's structure and coherence.",
  "01 用共同框架组织供应链研究": "01 Organise supply chain research around a common framework",
  "团队从生产战略、战略合作、数字化、全球供应链风险和可持续性五个方面展开，讨论拉动与看板、MTS/MTO 组合及供应商协同。我在整合内容时关注各部分是否围绕同一条业务逻辑：需求如何进入计划，物料如何支持生产，库存与交期怎样受到信息和供应变化影响。": "The team covered five areas: production strategy, strategic partnerships, digitalisation, global supply chain risks and sustainability, discussing pull systems and Kanban, MTS/MTO combinations and supplier coordination. When integrating the content, I checked that each section followed a consistent business logic: how demand feeds into planning, how materials support production, and how changes in information and supply affect inventory and lead times.",
  "02 将数字技术接到具体业务问题": "02 Connect digital technologies to specific business problems",
  "我的数字化分析围绕信息同步、物料可视化、预测和异常响应展开。EDI 对应订单与交期信息交换，IoT/RFID 对应物料状态与追溯，数字孪生用于讨论情景和风险，AI 分析工具用于预测或异常识别。技术名称之后必须说明使用场景、所需数据与可能影响的决策。": "My digitalisation analysis focused on information synchronisation, material visibility, forecasting and exception response. EDI relates to exchanging order and delivery information; IoT/RFID to material status and traceability; digital twins to scenarios and risks; and AI analytics tools to forecasting or anomaly detection. Naming a technology must be followed by an explanation of its use case, required data and the decisions it could inform.",
  "03 平衡低库存、韧性与数据质量": "03 Balance lean inventory, resilience and data quality",
  "低库存可以减少占用，也更依赖稳定交付和及时信息。研究因此同时考虑供应中断、关键物料、库存缓冲与协同响应。我在总结中保留了这个取舍：数字化方案应先明确问题和数据质量，再讨论工具；公开案例的研究认识不能写成自己已在 Toyota 完成系统实施。": "Lower inventory reduces capital tied up in stock but increases reliance on stable deliveries and timely information. The study therefore also considers supply disruptions, critical materials, inventory buffers and coordinated responses. I retained this trade-off in the conclusion: digitalisation proposals should first establish the problem and data quality, then consider tools. Insights from public case research should not be presented as systems I have implemented at Toyota.",
